#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:74
#. Diagram label
msgid "Answer, decline, or say nothing"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:104
#. Diagram label
msgid "Answered"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:94
#. Diagram label
msgid "Apply the stated default, and say so"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:69
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ask ONE question"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:120
#. Diagram label
msgid "declined"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Declined, or silent where no default is allowed. The record says what was asked and what is still open, so the next actor resumes rather than restarts. Never a guess."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:105
#. Diagram label
msgid "Default applied, and said so"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:87
#. Diagram label
msgid "Did the caller allow a default?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every option the agent could narrow the question to, each with what it costs and what it makes hard to undo. Narrow from context first: an option the agent could have ruled out itself wastes the reader's attention."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "First, and in the message itself: what the decision is, what depends on it, and what is already known — each fact with where it came from. A link is where somebody goes for more; it is never where the terms are defined."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Follow up, narrower"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:11
#. Diagram label
msgid "Human–agent discussion"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:90
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "In the form the caller asked for — for bootstrap's harness question, a document conforming to discussion.output.schema.json with determinedBy asked. Who answered (a person or an agent) is part of the record."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Judgement, exercised by the agent — which is why this gateway carries no computed decision. Whether an answer settles the matter is not computable from its text."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:59
#. Diagram label
msgid "Lay out the options, with what each costs"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Mark the option the agent would take and say why. Then say what happens if nobody answers: the default, when the caller allows one, or that the question stays open and the work stops, when it does not. Said now, so silence has a meaning both sides agreed to before it happened."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:119
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:117
#. Diagram label
msgid "no answer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:70
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One question, answerable by picking. With several decisions open, ask one in full and give a count for the rest. Uses whatever channel the caller is in — in bootstrap, the conversation the person is already in."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:95
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only the default stated in A_Recommend, only where the caller allows one, and recorded as assumed with the default named — never as the person's answer. The next message to the person says it was applied, so they can reverse it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:64
#. Diagram label
msgid "Recommend one, and say what happens with no answer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the answer, and who gave it"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:99
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record what is still open"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:45
#. Diagram label
msgid "Requestor"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:54
#. Diagram label
msgid "Say what is being decided, and why it matters now"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "settles it"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:52
#. Diagram label
msgid "Something only a person can supply is needed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "Still open, and said so"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The answer did not settle it: it named a kind rather than an option, or chose two. Ask once more, narrower, naming what the first answer left open. Once: an agent that keeps asking has stopped narrowing."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person who asked — or a sibling agent that already holds the answer. Answering, declining and saying nothing are all legitimate moves here, and each has its own end."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:75
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The Requestor's move. Declining is an answer. Saying nothing is not, and is what the recommendation's \"if there is no answer\" was for."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:115
#. Diagram label
msgid "unclear"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:78
#. Diagram label
msgid "What came back?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Whichever agent called this sub-process. It prepares the question, rules on whether an answer settles it, and records the outcome in the form its caller asked for. It never supplies the answer itself."
msgstr ""

#: processes/human-agent-discussion.bpmn:118
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
